---
import Studio from "../../layouts/Studio.astro";
import RelatedPosts from "../../components/RelatedPosts.astro";
import { SITE, DEFAULT_OG, CALENDLY_URL, fmtDate, iso, POSTS, authorNode, publisherNode, websiteNode, topicsForTags } from "../../lib/blog.mjs";
import { coverBase, coverSrcset, COVER_SIZES_POST } from "../../lib/images.mjs";

const slug = "page-speed-is-a-brand-statement";
const idx = POSTS.findIndex((p) => p.slug === slug);
const post = POSTS[idx];

const canonical = `${SITE}/blog/${slug}/`;
const ogImage = post.coverImage ? `${SITE}${post.coverImage}` : DEFAULT_OG;
const primaryTag = post.tags[0] || "Notes";
const readMins = post.readMins;
const showUpdated = post.updatedDate && +new Date(post.updatedDate) > +new Date(post.pubDate);
const updatedLabel = showUpdated ? `Updated ${fmtDate(post.updatedDate)}` : null;

const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BlogPosting",
      "@id": `${canonical}#post`,
      headline: post.title,
      description: post.description,
      datePublished: iso(post.pubDate),
      dateModified: iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate),
      author: authorNode(SITE),
      publisher: publisherNode(SITE),
      isPartOf: websiteNode(SITE),
      mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": canonical },
      image: ogImage,
      articleSection: primaryTag,
      keywords: post.tags.join(", "),
      // Resolves the free-text tags above to public concept identifiers, so a
      // parser knows "Astro" means the framework and "GEO" isn't geography.
      about: topicsForTags(post.tags),
      wordCount: 655,
      timeRequired: `PT${readMins}M`,
      speakable: {
        "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
        cssSelector: [".post-title", ".post-lead"],
      },
      inLanguage: "en",
      url: canonical,
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Blog", item: `${SITE}/blog/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: post.title, item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
---

<Studio
  title={post.seoTitle ?? `${post.title} · Divyansh Sood`}
  description={post.description}
  canonical={canonical}
  keywords={post.tags.join(", ")}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle={post.title}
  ogImage={ogImage}
  ogImageW={1200}
  ogImageH={750}
  articlePublished={iso(post.pubDate)}
  articleModified={iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate)}
  tags={post.tags}
  preloadImage={{ href: coverBase(post.coverImage), srcset: coverSrcset(post.coverImage), sizes: COVER_SIZES_POST }}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <main>
    <header class="post-hero">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span>{primaryTag}</span>
          <span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span>
          {updatedLabel && <span class="post-updated">{updatedLabel}</span>}
          <span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">{post.title}</h1>
        <p class="post-lead">{post.description}</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span>By Divyansh Sood</span><span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span><span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {post.coverImage && (
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <figure class="post-cover">
          <img
            src={coverBase(post.coverImage)}
            srcset={coverSrcset(post.coverImage)}
            sizes={COVER_SIZES_POST}
            alt={post.coverAlt ?? post.title}
            width="1200"
            height="750"
            fetchpriority="high"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>
    )}

    <article class="wrap narrow post-body">
      <p>Imagine walking into a boutique where the door sticks, the lights flicker for a second, and the rack you want slides open half a beat late.</p>
<p>Nothing is broken. But you’ve already formed an opinion about the brand.</p>
<p>That’s what a slow website does, every single visit. Speed isn’t a technical metric that lives in a developer’s dashboard — it’s the first physical sensation a customer has of your brand. And for a premium brand, a sluggish site quietly contradicts the entire pitch.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="slow-reads-as-cheap-even-subconsciously">Slow reads as “cheap,” even subconsciously</h2>
<p>People don’t think “Largest Contentful Paint is 4.2 seconds.” They think <em>this feels cheap</em> — and they don’t even know why.</p>
<p>Fast feels expensive. The instant tap, the image that’s already there, the page that responds before you finish the gesture — that’s the digital equivalent of a heavy door that swings on a perfect hinge. It signals care. It signals that someone sweated the details you can’t quite name.</p>
<p>If you charge a premium and your site stutters, you’re sending two contradictory messages. Customers believe the one they can feel.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="how-fast-is-fast-enough">How fast is fast enough</h2>
<p>Concrete targets, measured on a mid-range phone on mobile data — not your office wifi on a MacBook:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Largest Contentful Paint</strong> under 2.5s — the main content shows up fast</li>
<li><strong>Interaction to Next Paint</strong> under 200ms — taps feel instant</li>
<li><strong>Cumulative Layout Shift</strong> under 0.1 — nothing jumps as it loads</li>
<li><strong>Lighthouse mobile</strong> 90+ — the honest summary score</li>
</ul>
<p>Test your own at <a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev">pagespeed.web.dev</a> right now. If you’re in the 50s–70s — where most builder and plugin-heavy sites land — you have a brand problem wearing a technical costume.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="why-most-sites-are-slow-and-its-fixable">Why most sites are slow (and it’s fixable)</h2>
<p>Slowness is rarely the network’s fault. It’s usually self-inflicted:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Plugin and app sprawl</strong> — each one ships its own CSS and JavaScript that the browser has to download and run</li>
<li><strong>Unoptimised images</strong> — a 3MB hero on a phone is the single most common offender</li>
<li><strong>Render-blocking scripts</strong> — analytics, chat widgets, fonts, all loading before the page can paint</li>
<li><strong>Bloated themes</strong> — code for a hundred features you’ll never use, downloaded anyway</li>
</ul>
<p>A custom-coded site sidesteps all of it by shipping only what the page needs. When we built <a href="https://www.divyanshsood.com/projects/dharamshala-tours/">Dharamshala Tours</a>, 95%+ of traffic was on phones — so mobile speed wasn’t an optimisation pass at the end, it was the design constraint from the first line of code.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="speed-compounds-in-three-directions">Speed compounds in three directions</h2>
<p>Get it right and you’re paid back three ways at once:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Conversion.</strong> Faster pages keep more of the visitors you already paid to acquire — every second of delay leaks buyers.</li>
<li><strong>Rankings.</strong> Core Web Vitals are a direct Google ranking input. Fast pages rank higher, which means more free traffic, which compounds.</li>
<li><strong>Brand.</strong> Every visit reinforces “this company is sharp.” That impression follows you into the inbox, the checkout, and the referral.</li>
</ol>
<p>One investment, three returns — which is exactly why it’s worth doing properly instead of bolting a caching plugin onto a slow foundation.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-test-that-cuts-through-everything">The test that cuts through everything</h2>
<p>Open your site on your phone, on mobile data, after clearing the cache. Count the seconds until you can actually read and tap something.</p>
<p>If it’s more than two, your site is telling a story about your brand — and it isn’t the one on your About page.</p>
<p>Fast is a feeling. Premium brands can’t afford to feel slow.</p>
<hr>
<p><em>I’m Divyansh Sood. Every site I ship hits Lighthouse 90+ on a mid-range Android on mobile data — not because it’s technically impressive, because it’s the floor for a site that converts. 9 live builds. Speed is also how a small operator outranks a large one: <a href="/projects/baglamukhi-travels/">Baglamukhi Travels</a> averages position 5.7 on Google partly because the site is quick enough to deserve it. Where this matters most is <a href="/services/landing-page-design/">landing page design</a>. If a premium brand is reading this and seeing themselves in the “sluggish site contradicts the pitch” problem, <a href={CALENDLY_URL}>book a 15-min intro</a> and I’ll tell you what your current numbers actually are.</em></p>
      <div class="tags">{post.tags.map((t) => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
    </article>

    <RelatedPosts slug={slug} audience={post.audience} />

    <section class="post-foot-cta">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        {post.audience === "indian-smb" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something in India?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. WhatsApp reply in under an hour, 9 AM–9 PM IST — I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/919816091875" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Message me on WhatsApp <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : post.audience === "d2c-brand" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Building a brand a theme can't carry?</h2>
            <p>If your store has a model that off-the-shelf builders fight — hand-numbered drops, creator commerce, premium D2C — tell me about it. I read every brief personally.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something similar?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. I reply personally, usually within a couple of hours — and I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={CALENDLY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Book a 15-min intro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Studio>
